## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of schema evolution, per-tenant isolation, versioned data contracts, and end-to-end visibility under partial deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Versioned schemas with schema_version
- Backward/forward compatibility
- Ingest-time shims/transformations
- Region routing by tenant
- Privacy controls

## Code Example

```javascript
function normalizeEvent(raw) {
  const v = raw.schema_version ?? 1;
  if (v === 1) {
    return { tenant_id: raw.tenant_id, event_type: raw.event_type, timestamp: raw.timestamp, payload: raw.payload, session_id: null, latency_ms: null, schema_version: 2 };
  }
  return raw;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for backward compatibility when a deployed app carries mixed-v1 and v2 events?
- What are trade-offs of adding latency_ms at ingestion vs computing it at source?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests capability to design OTCA telemetry for model-monitoring with privacy, cross-region consistency, explainability, and controlled canary rollouts in a multi-tenant LLM service.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA telemetry across tenants with per-tenant residency
- Cross-region canonical events and immutable logs
- Explainability data collection and prompt redaction
- Drift detection and safety gating for canaries
- Testing for cross-tenant leakage and regulatory redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: event schema
type TelemetryEvent = {
  tenant_id: string;
  user_id_hash: string;
  model_id: string;
  prompt_type: string;
  latency_ms: number;
  token_count: number;
  bias_score: number;
  safety_flag: boolean;
  timestamp: string;
